  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather with warmer than average \ntemperatures through today.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure will remain to the east of the region. Due to the\ncenter of the high far off to the east, strong enough subsidence\nwill keep the region dry with the exception of a few showers \nand storms along the Quebec border this and tomorrow afternoon. \nIn addition, winds will remain fairly weak. Temperatures will \nremain warmer than average with upper 70s to mid 80s today. \nPatchy fog especially near the coast tonight as southerly \nmarine flow begins to increase ahead of the next system.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Rain later Wednesday into Thursday night,\nsteadiest Downeast.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nA slow moving vertically stacked low will cross New England \nWednesday night, then cross the southern Gulf of Maine Thursday\nthrough Thursday night. Rain should begin to expand across the \nregion later Wednesday into Wednesday night. The steadiest \nrains, and greater rain totals, Wednesday night through \nThursday night will occur across Downeast areas with decreasing \ntotals northward across the remainder of the forecast area. \nCould also have the slight chance of an afternoon thunderstorm \nThursday. Rain will then taper to showers Thursday night.",
